# THE SIFREI ROWS on Numbers 31 (THE NUMBERS WALK sitting 11 — MIDIAN, 2026-09-12): piskaot 157-158 by POSITION — the two between 156
# (30:14) and 159 (35:9); TWELVE rows at the shelf's row grain, each opened and verdicted in BOTH files; the middah named where the row argues
# by one (logic/MIDDOT.md). NO row on 31:25-54 (the shelf silent to 35:8). The rows' own defects (an attribution dropped three times, an arm
# reversed, an ancestor inserted, the Talmud and the Mishnah supplied, a rule about rules dropped, a name garbled, a citation and a book
# wrong, a lemma misquoted, an identity's leg run backward) read to their verses (RESEARCH_LOG.md).
from midian_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(157, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"TAKE THE VENGEANCE" — THE LEADERS\' PRAISE: THEY DO NOT DEPART THE WORLD UNTIL THEY TAKE ISRAEL\'S VENGEANCE, WHICH IS HIS; "FROM THE MIDIANITES" — BUT MOAB BEGAN (22:4, 22:7)? THE TWO DOGS AND THE WOLF: MOAB AND MIDIAN NEVER AT PEACE (GENESIS 36:35) UNTIL ISRAEL; THE MIDIANITES "CONTENDED" AND "COUNSELED". The row opens on the frame and the vengeance (the doubled root, one seat; Israel\'s vengeance His — the row\'s identification, the ink of 31:3 making it "the vengeance of the LORD" in Moses\' relay); asks why Midian and not Moab — the Balak chapter\'s ink answers (22:4 "Moab said to the elders of Midian", 22:7 "the elders of Moab and the elders of Midian"; the Hebrew row cites 22:7 alone, the English adds 22:4) — and reads the old feud off Genesis 36:35 ("Hadad who smote Midian in the field of Moab" — cut); the parable of the two dogs (the Balak runner\'s midian_joined row carries it from Sanhedrin 105a:13); the close reads the gentilic\'s letters twice — "they contended (midaynin) with Israel", "they counseled against Israel" (the two readings, the English reversing their order). THE INK: "the Midianites" with the article at two Bible seats — the command (25:17) and this (computed). The middot: the frame\'s "why this and not that" (the ink read for the priority), a paronomasia on the name (the narrative middot\' name-reading). The exam: Sanhedrin 105a (the two dogs), Bava Kamma 38a (Midian harassed, Moab spared — the Balak runner\'s cell).')
srow(157, 2, 'MATERIAL', '"AFTERWARD YOU SHALL BE GATHERED" — MOSES\' DEATH CONTINGENT ON THE WAR, AND HE WENT WITH ZEAL: "ARM" MEANS ZEAL, AS "ARMED SHALL YOU PASS OVER" (DEUTERONOMY 3:18); "TO GIVE THE VENGEANCE OF THE LORD" — NOT FLESH AND BLOOD\'S VENGEANCE BUT HIS WHO SPOKE AND THE WORLD WAS (NAHUM 1:2). The row reads the sequence clause as a condition on Moses\' life (the ink: "afterward" one seat; the promise of 27:13 cut) and Moses\' promptness off 31:3\'s first word — the lexical identity "arm"-"armed" with Deuteronomy 3:18 (the root\'s Torah seats all in 31-32 and that verse; computed); "the vengeance of the LORD" read as the row says, God\'s own (the phrase\'s three other seats Babylon\'s, computed). The middot: I2\'s lexical form (a word\'s sense fixed by its other seat), the plain sense of "afterward" as a sequence. The exam: the chronology — the war before Moses\' death (Deuteronomy 34), the tape\'s sequence constraint at the compile.')
srow(157, 3, 'MATERIAL', '"A THOUSAND TO A TRIBE, A THOUSAND TO A TRIBE" — 24,000, THE WORDS OF R. YISHMAEL; R. AKIVA: 12,000, AND "FOR ALL THE TRIBES OF ISRAEL" INCLUDES THE TRIBE OF LEVI; "THERE WERE DELIVERED OF THE THOUSANDS OF ISRAEL" — RIGHTEOUS MEN WHO GAVE THEMSELVES; R. NATAN: OTHERS HANDED THEM OVER — "THIS ONE IS FIT, LET HIM GO"; R. ELAZAR HAMODAI: THEY HID WHEN THEY HEARD MOSES\' DEATH HUNG ON THE WAR, AND WERE CONSCRIPTED PERFORCE. THE DOUBLED NUMERAL DISPUTE: R. Yishmael reads the doubling twice (two thousand a tribe — 24,000), R. Akiva once (12,000, the ink of 31:5\'s own sum; the parser\'s distributive reads the doubling as two thousands, and 31:5 states the product — computed); the Levi arm on "for ALL the tribes" (the phrase here and Joshua 22:14, computed) — THE TWO FILES DIFFER: the Hebrew "to INCLUDE the tribe of Levi", the English "to exclude", with R. Yishmael\'s name dropped and R. Akiva\'s proof phrase swapped (RESEARCH_LOG.md); the passive "were delivered" read three ways (the men\'s devotion, others\' choosing, conscription — Onkelos "were CHOSEN" beside R. Natan); Exodus 17:4 cut ("a little more and they will stone me"). THE INK: the deliver-root\'s two Torah seats both in this chapter (computed). The middot: the doubled word read as two (I2-adjacent, the "why repeated" form), the inclusion by "all" (the E-class amplifier), a passive read for its agent. The exam: the muster\'s count as a data row with two settings (12,000 / 24,000).')
srow(157, 4, 'MATERIAL', '"THEM AND PHINEHAS" — WEIGHED AS PHINEHAS, AND PHINEHAS AGAINST THEM ALL; WHY PHINEHAS AND NOT ELEAZAR? TO AVENGE HIS MOTHER\'S FATHER — "AND THE MEDANITES SOLD HIM TO EGYPT" (GENESIS 37:36); "THE HOLY VESSELS" — THE ARK (4:20); "IN HIS HAND" — HIS DOMAIN (21:26, GENESIS 24:10). The row reads "them and Phinehas" as an equation of weight; explains Phinehas by descent — the Hebrew\'s proof is Joseph\'s sale, so "his mother\'s father" is JOSEPH (Phinehas\'s mother of Putiel\'s daughters, Exodus 6:25), and THE ENGLISH INSERTS "(Yithro, viz. Shemot 2:16)" — a different ancestor with a citation the Hebrew lacks, against its own proof (RESEARCH_LOG.md); and the proof text\'s own word is "the MEDANITES" (Genesis 37:36 — Keturah\'s other son, 25:2) where 37:28 has "Midianite men, merchants" (computed): the Sifrei reads the brothers as one; "the holy vessels" = the ark by the identity "the holy" with 4:20 (cut); "his hand" = his domain by two seats (I2\'s lexical form). THE INK: "and the holy vessels" the Kohathites\' charge (3:31); the trumpets\' one narrative seat — the war clause of 10:9 run (computed; the row is silent on the trumpets). The middot: I2 (the holy; the hand). The exam: Sotah 43a (Putiel = Joseph and Jethro — the ancestor\'s two readings).')
srow(157, 5, 'MATERIAL', '"THEY WARRED AGAINST MIDIAN" — FROM FOUR SIDES; R. NATAN: A FOURTH LEFT TO FLEE; "THE FIVE KINGS" NAMED AGAIN — ONE IN COUNSEL, ONE IN PUNISHMENT; BALAAM BY THE SWORD — HIS FULL REWARD FOR HIS COUNSEL; R. NATAN: BY A COURT (JOSHUA 13:22); THE CITIES ARE THEIR IDOLATRY, THE CASTLES THEIR PALACES OR THEIR SENTINELS; "THEY BROUGHT TO MOSES" — HONEST MEN, AGAINST ACHAN; MOSES AND ELEAZAR WENT OUT BECAUSE THE YOUTHS SNATCHED THE SPOIL (ABBA CHANIN, R. ELAZAR); "MOSES WAS WROTH" — THE STIGMA HANGS ON THE GREAT; PHINEHAS: AS YOU CHARGED US SO WE DID; "BY THE WORD OF BALAAM" — THE COUNSEL: THEIR GOD HATES LEWDNESS. The longest row runs 31:7 to 31:16: the siege\'s sides (R. Natan\'s mercy-gate); the five kings\' second naming as the equal-punishment rule; Balaam\'s "full reward" for the counsel of 24:14 — "when you were six hundred thousand you could not withstand them" (the ink\'s 600,000, computed) — and R. NATAN\'S COURT: the Hebrew "by a court they killed him", citing Joshua 13:22\'s "among their slain" — THE ENGLISH SUPPLIES THE TALMUD\'S "four judicial death penalties" (Sanhedrin 106b; RESEARCH_LOG.md); the cities and the castles — the Hebrew assigns the idolatry to "their cities in their dwellings" and two readings to the castles; the English (with ONKELOS "their houses of worship") puts the idolatry on the castles; honesty against Achan (Joshua 7:1 cut); the youths (the name R. ELAZAR in the Hebrew, "R. Eliezer" in the English); the great bear the offense; Phinehas\'s answer; Balaam\'s counsel spelled out — Egypt\'s six hundred chariots (Exodus 14:7 cut), "the LORD will war for you" (14:14 cut) turned to "He turned into their foe" (Isaiah 63:10) and "He has become as an enemy" (Lamentations 2:5). THE INK: "the kings of Midian" four Bible seats — Gideon\'s the others; the five names at Joshua 13:21 as Sihon\'s princes; "by the word of Balaam" one seat — ONKELOS "by the counsel" (computed). The middot: the second naming read (the "why repeated" form), the retelling read for the mode (Joshua 13:22), the frame read for a cause (31:13). The exam: Sanhedrin 106a-b (Balaam\'s death — the Balak runner\'s balaam_death row, two settings), Sanhedrin 82a-b.')
srow(157, 6, 'MATERIAL', '"EVERY WOMAN WHO HAS KNOWN A MAN BY LYING WITH A MALE, KILL" — THE ONE WHO HAS LAIN, OR THE ONE FIT TO LIE? 31:18\'S "WHO HAVE NOT KNOWN" DECIDES: FIT FOR INTERCOURSE, THOUGH SHE HAS NOT; WHY THE SECOND "KILL"? TO CLOSE THE SUBJECT — THE WORDS OF R. YISHMAEL; ANOTHER READING: THE A-FORTIORI (THE FIT ONE KILLED — THE ONE WHO HAS LAIN ALL THE MORE) WOULD PUNISH BY INFERENCE, SO "KILL" IS WRITTEN, TO TEACH THAT WE DO NOT PUNISH BY INFERENCE; "THE LITTLE ONES AMONG THE WOMEN... KEEP ALIVE" — R. SHIMON BEN YOCHAI: A PROSELYTE CONVERTED UNDER THREE YEARS AND A DAY IS FIT FOR THE PRIESTHOOD. The row runs the "how do I uphold both verses" form on 31:17 against 31:18 (fit for intercourse the criterion), then reads the verse\'s SECOND "kill" (the verse opens and closes on the verb — computed) two ways: R. Yishmael\'s structural rule (a repeated verb closes a paragraph — "to interrupt the matter"), and THE RULE ABOUT RULES — AIN ONSHIN MIN HA-DIN, "we do not punish by inference": an a-fortiori may not ground a penalty, so the ink must say "kill" itself — THE ENGLISH DROPS THIS READING WHOLE and R. Yishmael\'s name, and cites "(31:7)" for 31:17 (RESEARCH_LOG.md); R. Shimon ben Yochai\'s ruling on the priesthood from "keep alive for yourselves". THE INK: Judges 21:11-12 runs the sentence with its phrase and its number (computed). The middot: the "uphold both verses" form, THE REFUSED A-FORTIORI ON A PENALTY (MIDDOT.md\'s case law: I1 barred from punishment — Sanhedrin 54a, Makkot 5b), the structural "closing" reading. The exam: Yevamot 60b (the proselyte under three — R. Shimon ben Yochai), Sanhedrin 54a, Makkot 5b.')
srow(157, 7, 'MATERIAL', '"ENCAMP OUTSIDE THE CAMP SEVEN DAYS" — WHY? FROM 19:14\'S "ALL THAT IS IN THE TENT" I MIGHT INCLUDE STRAW AND TWIGS; THEY DO NOT COME INTO THE CATEGORY OF UNCLEANNESS; "YOU AND YOUR CAPTIVES" — AS YOU ARE CHILDREN OF THE COVENANT, SO YOUR CAPTIVES. The row ties the seven days to the heifer\'s tent (19:14 cut) and repeats piska 126\'s exclusion (the Chukat ledger\'s row: straw, twigs, wood, stones — "the four vessels of the Midian spoil" named there); THE ENGLISH REPLACES THE CONCLUSION WITH "(see Chukath #126)" (RESEARCH_LOG.md); "you and your captives" read as the captives\' sprinkling — covenant-children for the rite (the English\'s parenthesis on the girls under three its gloss). THE INK: "you and your captives" one seat; the schedule "on the third day and on the seventh day" at 19:12, 19:19 and 31:19 (computed). The middot: E-class exclusion (the "I might think" refused), the likening "as you, so your captives" (an E-class analogy on the pronoun pair). The exam: the heifer runner\'s water of separation by CALL (the compile\'s edge chukat).')
srow(157, 8, 'MATERIAL', '"EVERY GARMENT AND EVERY VESSEL OF SKIN" — WHY? LEVITICUS 11:32 SAYS "SKIN OR SACK"; WHENCE EVERY WORK OF GOATS? THE A-FORTIORI REFUSED BOTH WAYS; "GARMENT" IS FREED TO FORM THE IDENTITY: GARMENT HERE, GARMENT THERE — AS HERE GOAT-WORK IS LIKE SACK, SO THERE; AS THERE SPUN AND WOVEN, SO HERE: THE BAND, THE BELT AND THE ASS\'S GIRTH IN; CORDS AND ROPES OUT. The chapter\'s one full I2: Leviticus 11:32\'s list (wood, garment, skin, SACK) against 31:20\'s (garment, skin, GOAT-WORK, wood — computed), the a-fortiori refused ("do we derive from the stringent to be lenient and stringent with it?"), "garment" declared FREED (mufneh) and the identity run two ways — goat-work to the creeping thing\'s law, spun-and-woven to the dead\'s; THE TWO FILES RUN THE FIRST LEG IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS: the Hebrew "as the garment said THERE has goat-work like sack, so HERE" — but goat-work is 31:20\'s word, not Leviticus\'s; the English "as here, so there", the direction the ink allows (RESEARCH_LOG.md); the Greek loans for the band and the belt. THE INK: "work of goats" one seat; "sack" two Torah seats — Jacob\'s and 11:32\'s (computed). The middot: I2 WITH THE FREED-WORD CONDITION (MIDDOT.md under I2: no identity of one\'s own, Pesachim 66a; a freed word licenses), I1 refused twice. The exam: Shabbat 64a (the goat-work — spun and woven; the band and the belt), Kelim.')
srow(157, 9, 'MATERIAL', '"AND ELEAZAR THE PRIEST SAID... THIS IS THE STATUTE OF THE TORAH WHICH THE LORD COMMANDED MOSES" — IT WAS FORGOTTEN BY MOSES: HE CAME TO ANGER AND CAME TO ERROR; R. ELAZAR: IN THREE PLACES — LEVITICUS 10:16, NUMBERS 20:10, 31:14; OTHERS: MOSES GAVE ELEAZAR LEAVE TO SPEAK IN HIS LIFETIME; R. YOSHIYAH: "WHICH THE LORD COMMANDED MOSES" — HE SAID THE THING IN THE NAME OF ITS SAYER (ESTHER 2:22). The row explains the priest\'s voice on the heifer\'s law (the phrase "this is the statute of the Torah" at 19:2 and here alone — computed): anger begets forgetting, at three seats — the sin offering (Leviticus 10:16, cut), Meribah (20:10, cut — where the ink carries no wrath-verb; the wrath-verb with Moses as subject stands at Exodus 16:20, Leviticus 10:16, 31:14, computed: the Sifrei\'s three share two), and this; or the succession\'s courtesy; or the attribution rule — THE ENGLISH DROPS R. YOSHIYAH\'S NAME (RESEARCH_LOG.md). The middot: a rule about the lawgiver (anger → error, read off the frames), the attribution rule (Esther 2:22 the exemplar — "in the name of its sayer" MIDDOT.md\'s conduct row). The exam: Pesachim 66b (anger and forgetting — Resh Lakish\'s three), Megillah 15a (in the name of its sayer).')
srow(158, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"ONLY THE GOLD AND THE SILVER" — VESSELS, OR RAW LUMPS? ISRAEL\'S DEAD AND MIDIAN\'S SLAIN BOTH DEFILE: AS ISRAEL\'S DEAD DEFILE VESSELS AND NOT LUMPS, SO MIDIAN\'S; R. YOSE HAGELILI: "ONLY" DIVIDES. The row reads the metals list as finished vessels by an analogy between two defilers (the "you reason" form — a common feature: both defile), or by the limiter "only" (E-class; "only" at 31:22 and 31:23, computed). THE INK: the six metals in one verse, tin\'s one Torah seat, lead\'s two (computed). The middot: the analogy on a shared feature (the narrative middot\' binyan-av form), the E-class limiter. The exam: Avodah Zarah 75b (the vessels of the gentiles), Kelim 11:1 (metal vessels — from here).')
srow(158, 2, 'MATERIAL', '"EVERYTHING THAT COMES INTO THE FIRE YOU SHALL PASS THROUGH THE FIRE" — THE POTS, THE KNIVES, THE SPITS AND THE GRILLS, BECAUSE OF THE GENTILES\' ABSORPTIONS; "AND ALL THAT DOES NOT COME INTO THE FIRE" — THE CUPS, THE FLASKS AND THE KETTLES; THE IMMERSION BY A-FORTIORI: IF WHAT NEEDS NO SPRINKLING NEEDS IMMERSION, WHAT NEEDS SPRINKLING ALL THE MORE. The row lists the vessels of fire and of water (five and five in the Hebrew, Greek and Aramaic names among them) and names the reason — "the absorptions of the gentiles" (the kashering rule\'s ground, the Sifrei\'s own label of the data channel); THE ENGLISH SUPPLIES THE MISHNAH\'S SPLIT — "knives, spits and grills are whitened; pots and kettles boiled" (Avodah Zarah 5:12\'s words) where the Hebrew lists all five under the fire with no split — and gives one a-fortiori for the Hebrew\'s two, the second garbled (RESEARCH_LOG.md). THE INK: "pass through the fire" and "pass through water" one seat each; "the water of sprinkling" the heifer\'s, four seats in 19 and 31 (computed). The middot: I1 (the immersion from the sprinkling), the list as specification. The exam: Mishnah Avodah Zarah 5:12, Avodah Zarah 75b-76b (the vessels of Midian — the whole sugya\'s seat), Pesachim 30b.')
srow(158, 3, 'MATERIAL', '"WASH YOUR GARMENTS ON THE SEVENTH DAY AND BE CLEAN" — WHY? SINCE "SLAIN BY THE SWORD" IS SPOKEN OF, SCRIPTURE TEACHES THAT THE SWORD IS UNCLEAN AND ITS TOUCHER UNCLEAN SEVEN DAYS — VESSELS AND MAN; VESSELS, MAN AND VESSELS — FROM "WASH YOUR GARMENTS"; "AND AFTERWARD COME INTO THE CAMP" — AS HERE HE IS BARRED FROM THE CAMP, SO THERE (19:19); AS THERE "UNTIL THE EVENING", SO HERE. The row derives the sword\'s seven days (the Chukat ledger\'s rows 127:1 and 130:1 carry it from this verse) and the chain vessels-man-vessels from the garments\' washing, then likens 31:24 and 19:19 BOTH WAYS (the camp\'s bar exported to the heifer, the evening imported here — the two-way likening the vows\' footer also used); THE HEBREW MISQUOTES 31:24 as "and they shall wash their garments" (the Levites\' form, 8:7 — computed) for "and you shall wash your garments", and its citation "(19:19) \'slain by the sword\'" names 19:16\'s phrase; THE ENGLISH CITES "Vayikra 19:19" for Bamidbar 19:19 (RESEARCH_LOG.md). THE INK: "afterward come into the camp" one seat, the leper\'s and the heifer-priest\'s its kin; "be clean at evening" 19:19 (computed). The middot: the likening (hekkesh — no I-code; MIDDOT.md\'s case law) two ways, the inference of the chain. The exam: Pesachim 14b, Nazir 53b-54b (the sword as the slain — "the sword is like the slain"), Chullin 3a; the heifer runner\'s cells by CALL.')
assert sorted(S) == [(p, r) for p in PISKAOT for r in range(1, SIF_ROWS[p] + 1)], sorted(S)
